<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A2.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Output of final 6 MCMC samples comparing U-LATINO to LATINO. The ground truth <math id="A2.F8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is taken from the PROBES hold-out validation data and observation kernel <math id="A2.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{k}}\in K_{\text{4h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>4h</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{k}}\in K_{\text{4h}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.3 </span>Comparison on SBM Prior Data</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a further benchmark for the models considered in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Radio Interferometry ‣ 4 Numerical Experiments ‣ Deep unfolding of MCMC kernels: scalable, modular &amp; explainable GANs for high-dimensional posterior sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, we present here a separate comparison using a synthetic PROBES test set. For this data, we generate 128 ground-truth images from the IRIS SBM prior for the purpose of testing each model. A qualitative comparison for a typical reconstruction from this data is shown in <a href="#A2.F9" title="In B.2.3 Comparison on SBM Prior Data ‣ B.2 Additional Results on PROBES data ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Deep unfolding of MCMC kernels: scalable, modular &amp; explainable GANs for high-dimensional posterior sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, and quantitative metrics, averaged over the test set are shown in <a href="#A2.T4" title="In B.2.3 Comparison on SBM Prior Data ‣ B.2 Additional Results on PROBES data ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Deep unfolding of MCMC kernels: scalable, modular &amp; explainable GANs for high-dimensional posterior sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. For the quantitative results, we observe a slight improvement in all metrics for each method compared to <a href="#S4.T2" title="In 4.2.6 Results ‣ 4.2 Radio Interferometry ‣ 4 Numerical Experiments ‣ Deep unfolding of MCMC kernels: scalable, modular &amp; explainable GANs for high-dimensional posterior sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. This can be attributed to less background noise in the SBM prior data, along with the IRIS and LATINO models using a prior <math id="A2.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> which matches exactly the generating distribution for images in this test set. Compared to U-LATINO, the zero-shot LATINO attains a higher SSIM score and correlation between posterior standard-deviation and residual error on this dataset image. We attribute this to the zero-shot model over-fitting to the prior data, combined with the fact that U-LATINO was not fine-tuned on images from this SBM prior.</p>
</div>
